## 3. Services (`shell/MatShell/Services/*.qml`)

Every service is `pragma Singleton` + `Singleton { id: root }`, registered in `qmldir`. Properties marked **ro** are `readonly property`. A service starts no poller until a consumer calls its `sample()`/`refresh()` or binds a `*Active` flag (R07).

### 3.1 `ConfigService`
Owns `~/.config/mat-shell/config.json` through `FileView { watchChanges: true; atomicWrites: true }`. Parses with `JSON.parse` and `barConfig.normalizeConfig`. It does not use `JsonAdapter`, because the bar tree is dynamic.

`Config` (schema, `schemaVersion: 1`):

```json
{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "appearance": { "darkMode": true, "surfaceMode": "frosted_tonal_glass", "desktopMode": "tiling", "densityMode": "comfortable",
                  "schemeVariant": "scheme-tonal-spot", "themedIcons": true, "widgetScale": 1.0 },
  "theme": { "wallpaper": "" },
  "bars": [ "Bar objects (§2.5)" ],
  "widgets": { "enabled": true },
  "notifications": { "dnd": false, "toastCorner": "top-right" },
  "keybinds": { "<actionId>": ["<chord>"] },
  "animations": { "expressiveSprings": true },
  "accessibility": { "reducedMotion": false, "reducedTransparency": false, "highContrast": false, "textScale": 1.0, "confirmByHold": true },
  "ui": { "lastSettingsPage": "appearance" }
}
```

| Member | Contract |
|---|---|
| ro `config: var` | the current normalized `Config` (replaced as a whole on every change, so bindings update) |
| ro `error: string` | `""`, or `"config.json has an error on line N"` after an invalid external edit (the last good config stays active) |
| ro `loaded: bool` | true after the first successful read or first-run write |
| `get(path: string): var` | dotted path read (`"notifications.dnd"`) |
| `set(path: string, value: var): void` | dotted path write → new `config` → debounced write (300ms) |
| `transaction(label: string, fn: function): void` | runs `fn` with `set` calls batched into one undo entry and one write |
| `undo(): bool` | restores the previous entry (max 50 entries) |
| ro `undoLabel: string` | label of the entry `undo()` would restore |
| `addBar(): string` | first edge with capacity (rule order `top, bottom, left, right`), widgets `launcher, workspaces / clock / controlCenter`; returns the id |
| `updateBar(id: string, patch: object): void` | shallow-merge, then `normalizeBar` |
| `removeBar(id: string): void` | one undo entry |
| `applyPreset(name: string): void` | replaces `bars` (one undo entry) |
| `removeWidget(barId, section, index): void` | one undo entry |
| `setWidgetOptions(barId, section, index, options: object): void` | stores `diffFromDefaults(type, options)`; an empty result removes the `options` key |
| `restoreLastGood(): void` | rewrites the file from the last good config |

First run (file missing): write `defaultConfig()` with the dock's `apps.options.pinned` = `firstRunPinned(FIRST_RUN_PIN_GROUPS, id => DesktopEntries.byId(id) !== null)`.

