## 6. Bar Widget Contract (`bar/widgets/*Widget.qml`)

`BarWidgetLoader` (spec `02-bar-widgets.md` §8) loads `BarWidgetRegistry.source(type)` and binds these properties into the item. Every widget declares all of them, even if unused:

| Property | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `options` | `var` | raw stored options (never read directly; G13) |
| `vertical` | `bool` | host bar orientation |
| `barEdge` | `string` | `"top"\|"right"\|"bottom"\|"left"` |
| `barId` | `string` | host bar id (for `Configure bar…`) |
| `edgeReach`, `crossSlack`, `pillSize` | `real` | hit-area geometry from the loader |
| `overflowStep` | `int` | set by `BarLayout` (§2.7); `0` = full |
| ro `overflowSteps` | `int` | number of degrade steps this widget supports (`0` for never-hidden widgets) |

Each widget:
1. Declares `readonly property var opt: BarWidgetRegistry.resolve("<type>", options, vertical ? "vertical" : "horizontal")` when the type has options.
2. Popover openers call `ShellState.registerTrigger(name, this)` in `Component.onCompleted` and pass `this` to `togglePopover`.
3. Sets `accessibleName` and `tooltipText` from live state (`"Wi-Fi Home-5G · Volume 72% · Battery 86%"`).
4. Uses `font.features: Tokens.typography.tabularFeatures` on every live number.
5. Opens the widget menu on `rightClicked()` (`01-architecture.md` §5.2).

